{"meta": {"limit": 100, "next": null, "offset": 0, "previous": null, "total_count": 31}, "objects": [{"abstract": "   A number of extensions are proposed in the TLS working group that\n   carry no interesting information except the 1-bit indication that a\n   certain optional feature is supported.  Such extensions take 4 octets\n   each.  This document defines a flags extension that can provide such\n   indications at an average marginal cost of 1 bit each.  More\n   precisely, it provides as many flag extensions as needed at 4 + the\n   order of the last set bit divided by 8.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags/", "expires": "2024-01-24T19:19:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 337337, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags", "note": "", "notify": "Christopher Wood <caw@heapingbits.net>", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/337337/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/caw@heapingbits.net/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2023-07-23T19:19:07Z", "title": "A Flags Extension for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   A number of extensions are proposed in the TLS working group that\n   carry no interesting information except the 1-bit indication that a\n   certain optional feature is supported.  Such extensions take 4 octets\n   each.  This document defines a flags extension that can provide such\n   indications at an average marginal cost of 1 bit each.  More\n   precisely, it provides as many flag extensions as needed at 4 + the\n   order of the last set bit divided by 8.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags/", "expires": "2024-01-24T19:19:07Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 355789, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags", "note": "", "notify": "Christopher Wood <caw@heapingbits.net>, sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/355789/", "rev": "12", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/2/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-03-12T14:05:56Z", "title": "A Flags Extension for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/name/doctypename/draft/", "uploaded_filename": "", "words": null}, {"abstract": "   A number of extensions are proposed in the TLS working group that\n   carry no interesting information except the 1-bit indication that a\n   certain optional feature is supported.  Such extensions take 4 octets\n   each.  This document defines a flags extension that can provide such\n   indications at an average marginal cost of 1 bit each.  More\n   precisely, it provides as many flag extensions as needed at 4 + the\n   order of the last set bit divided by 8.\n", "ad": null, "doc": "/api/v1/doc/document/draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags/", "expires": "2024-09-17T21:01:24Z", "external_url": "", "group": "/api/v1/group/group/1326/", "id": 356247, "intended_std_level": "/api/v1/name/intendedstdlevelname/ps/", "keywords": "[]", "name": "draft-ietf-tls-tlsflags", "note": "", "notify": "Christopher Wood <caw@heapingbits.net>, sean@sn3rd.com", "pages": 9, "resource_uri": "/api/v1/doc/dochistory/356247/", "rev": "13", "rfc_number": null, "shepherd": "/api/v1/person/email/sean@sn3rd.com/", "states": ["/api/v1/doc/state/1/", "/api/v1/doc/state/150/", "/api/v1/doc/state/145/"], "std_level": null, "stream": "/api/v1/name/streamname/ietf/", "tags": [], "time": "2024-03-16T21:01:24Z", "title": "A Flags Extension for TLS 1.3", "type": "/api/v1/na